# A course about Git ought to have one of these.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide what is text, store it with LF in the repository,
# and check it out with the platform's convention. This is the setting the
# chapter on repository structure recommends over `core.autocrlf`, because it
# travels with the repository instead of living in each contributor's config.
* text=auto

# The transcripts under utilities/snippets are compared byte for byte by
# utilities/scenario.sh --check, so they must never be touched by any filter.
utilities/snippets/*.txt -text

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on Windows checkouts or they will not run.
*.sh text eol=lf
utilities/git-object-read       text eol=lf
utilities/git-objects-print-all text eol=lf

# Binaries: never munge, never try to diff.
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.psd  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
